  "adaptations": [
    "Remove only the fixed globalThis export and outer IIFE; retain all original library helpers, class methods, aliases and static BDCompare assignment.",
    "Add erased types and declare fields so original constructor assignment order remains unchanged. Successful instances have initialized base/decimals; the original bigint-input path still reads the absent _decimals before assignment and throws.",
    "Write isNaN(Number(n)) for number|string inputs, explicitly expressing the original global isNaN primitive numeric coercion.",
    "Use a checked BigDenary receiver in the default comparator so its type can coexist with the original number-result Object.is comparison. Unsupported default numeric receivers still throw TypeError.",
    "After each original first/last comparison, observe the last result as a decimal string and mix its code units plus length into an unsigned multiply-by-31 checksum. Retain at most six strings; every full iteration contributes.",
    "Keep original full inputs and a single stateless-valid Benchmark outside work. Run the original validate after the requested complete iterations. No RNG, native numeric shortcut, changed precision or reduced repeat count."
  ],
